   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed package: S1 is strict on reporting but omits customer notification, while S2 avoids a sales ban for the Hearth 10 by turning the 5% threshold into a corrective-action trigger. S3 and S4 settle at 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression, and S5 adopts a mandatory model-specific recall at 8/100k with 24-hour customer notice. The overall effect favors Northwind on S2, S3, and S5, while Halcyon secures its S4 red line and customer access to test results."
 },
